# JupyterLab Workbench

This workbench is managed by Ansible for `{{ inventory_hostname }}`.

## Web access

- URL: `{{ dev_jupyterlab_workbench_operator_url }}`
- Password: `{{ dev_jupyterlab_workbench_password_plain }}`

## What to open first

- `langfuse-cookbooks/` contains the official Langfuse recipe notebooks from
  `{{ dev_jupyterlab_workbench_cookbooks_repo }}`
- upstream checkout lives at `{{ dev_jupyterlab_workbench_repo_checkout_dir }}`
- `.env` is the managed runtime environment with the local homelab endpoints
  and keys needed by the recipes

## Local service wiring

- Langfuse: `{{ dev_jupyterlab_workbench_langfuse_host }}`
- LiteLLM: `{{ dev_jupyterlab_workbench_openai_base_url }}`

## Notes

- `OPENAI_API_KEY` is wired to the local LiteLLM proxy key so OpenAI-compatible
  notebooks can target the homelab gateway when they honor `OPENAI_BASE_URL`.
- `OPENAI_MODEL` defaults to `{{ dev_jupyterlab_workbench_openai_model }}` for
  local OpenAI-compatible client usage through LiteLLM.
- If a notebook expects a real upstream provider key, set it in `.env` after
  deciding which provider you want to use.
